 "verdict": "The owner's 'heavy wind' is gone. No looping ambience-bus cue reads as heavy wind or a repeating whoosh as heard: the beds are steady, band-limited air (swell 1.4-2.4 LU, 250 Hz-2 kHz band moving 2.9-4.2 dB, no gust, no band sweep, below the quiet music in every third-octave), the BRIDGE updraft is a steady fixed-band rush heard only at the deck edges 17.8-25 LU under the music, and the pit presences are still low drones 19.3-21.3 LU under the music. Every level bar holds live on every map and spot measured, and each map keeps a sense of place in calm (the bed 11.3-16.8 LU under the music, a positional detail at each landmark). Two minor loop-seam holes and one ungated high-band rustle remain; none of them is wind and none is a blocker.",
 "method": [
  "audio/build.py --gates over the shipped files (through heavy.py): PASS, every ambience gate inside its bar (log: scratchpad gates.log).",
  "probe_audio_runtime.mjs match on rift_coop seeds 3/7/11/21, bridge_standard and fray_standard seed 3 (420 s each, through heavy.py, dev server localhost:5190 on HEAD).",
  "probe_audio_runtime.mjs pits on rift_coop seeds 3/7/11/21 (the new mode).",
  "A spot probe of my own (scratchpad, modeled on pits mode, nothing in the repo edited) put the engine listener on named spots for 14-26 s with every objective spawned early: RIFT lanes top/mid/bottom, two jungle canopy points, two river shallows points, 10 m east and north of each objective pit, and the busiest emitter point; BRIDGE deck middle, deck quarter, two deck edges on updraft points, the busiest point; FRAY centre, edge, lantern, bunting and busiest point. I metered the music, ambience and sfx buses and every emitter's gain node, K-weighted, and recorded the raw ambience bus (L/R) at 6 spots to decode.",
  "Decoded every ambience-bus cue in audio/out (.ogg, cross-checked against .m4a at the seams): BS.1770 integrated level as played (gain), 3 s short-term swell over the loop, 250 Hz-2 kHz 0.5 s band envelope range and circular autocorrelation from 2 s to half the loop, the spectral centroid track and its correlation with level (the whoosh signature), share of energy above 2 and 4 kHz and below 200 Hz, spectral flatness at 200 Hz-4 kHz, 80-160 Hz third-octaves against the map music's quietest stretch, 22 third-octaves against the four quietest 3 s frames of each map's music, holes at the loop seam, L/R correlation and mono-sum loss."
