 "rawBusNotes": "At calm spots the bus as heard holds a short-term swell of 1.35-2.31 LU and a band range of 2.9-4.8 dB, with no lag repeating at >= 0.6 while it moves >= 3 dB (RIFT canopy 0.65 at 12 s over only 2.9 dB). It keeps 2.1-6.2 % of its energy above 2 kHz and is not anti-correlated (L/R +0.39 to +0.80, mono loss 0.5-1.6 dB). The 6.2-7.4 LU swells at the FRAY lantern, FRAY busiest and RIFT busiest spots come from the fight duck releasing over 3.5 s in windows that were 8-62 % ducked. That is the designed 'world fades back in', not a whoosh in any cue, and it moves the bus only while it sits 12+ LU under the music.",
