 "soundDesignerJudgement": {
  "amb_rift_air": "A warm, steady low breath (centroid 456 Hz, peak 275 Hz, 0.7 % above 2 kHz). Swell 1.9 LU, band 2.9 dB, no gust and no sweep (the centroid moves 425-497 Hz). It plays 12.5 LU under the RIFT music by file and stays at least 4.9 dB under the music's quietest frames in every third-octave. The 125 Hz roar is gone (-62.7 dB vs -41.4 dB music). Reads as valley air or room tone, not heavy wind.",
  "amb_bridge_air": "The intended 'high wind', held soft: steady (swell 2.4 LU, band 4.2 dB, ac 0.35), with a faint 760 Hz whistle. At most 2.5 dB under the quiet music, at 2 kHz, so it is audible as air on the bridge, as the map calls for. Live it sits 13.2-21 LU under the music. A player could call it wind, rightly, but not heavy wind and not a repeating whoosh.",
  "amb_bridge_updraft": "A steady fixed-band rush (centroid 658-730 Hz, swell 0.87 LU, band 2.3 dB). It is wind by design but local: at full only within 5 m of its 12 points, 17.8-25.4 LU under the music live. Fine.",
  "amb_fray_murmur": "A far fair (36 s, random bells). Swell 1.4 LU, band 3.0 dB, ac 0.50 at 15 s over only 3 dB, so no audible cycle. No wind character (centroid 867 Hz, flatness 0.17). There is a -1.7 dB level step across the seam, masked.",
  "amb_rift_canopy": "Sparse leaf patter (18.4 % above 2 kHz, flatness 0.54, swell 1.4 LU). Not wind. It carries a 110 ms digital-silence hole at its loop seam, every 12 s (see problems).",
  "amb_rift_water": "Bubbles and laps over a fixed-band murmur (band 4.6 dB, ac 0.10). Not a wash swell. Fine.",
  "amb_fray_lantern": "Paper rustle plus high chimes. In practice it is a continuous high-band rustle: 59 % above 2 kHz, 83 % of its >2 kHz energy within 6 dB of its floor, flatness 0.54. It is classed as a non-wash, so the 25 % HF cap never reads it. Hiss or rustle, not wind. It also has a 70 ms seam hole every 8 s.",
  "amb_lamp_flame / amb_fray_bunting / amb_bridge_creak / amb_rift_insects / amb_wren": "Local details. None continuous noise with a swell. Insects are tonal chirps at 4.3 kHz (flatness 0.006). Fine.",
  "u_longshade_presence / u_sunsplinter_presence": "Still drones (swell 0.96 / 0.83 LU, band 2.3 / 1.6 dB, no >2 kHz content, mono). 19.3-21.3 LU under the music live on their pit edges. No breathing. Fine.",
  "m_gorge_gust": "Not a loop (sudden death only, 3 s). L/R +0.90, mono loss 0.23 dB, -33.7 LUFS as played. Fine."
 },
 "senseOfPlace": "Kept on all three maps. RIFT: valley air, plus leaf patter in the jungle, water and insects at the river, and a drone at each pit. BRIDGE: soft high wind, plus a rush at the deck edges, creaks and lamp flame. FRAY: a far murmur with bells, plus lanterns, bunting and lamps. In calm the bed sits 11-16 LU under the music, quiet but present. It is near-inaudible only under fight ducks, which is the genre norm.",
 "problems": [
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "cue": "amb_rift_canopy",
   "what": "A 110 ms run of digital silence at the loop seam (the last 60 ms and first 25 ms of the file are zero, ogg and m4a alike), so the patter's continuous component drops out every 12 s (pitchVar 0). Live at a canopy point the 500 Hz-10 kHz band of the bus dips 6.4-7.2 dB at 1.33, 13.30 and 25.08 s, exactly the loop period. Likely cause: the patter's grains are scattered without wrapping around the loop, and the build's edge gate rewards quiet edges. Fix: wrap the scatter (add_at wrap=True) so the seam carries grains."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "cue": "amb_fray_lantern",
   "what": "A 70 ms hole at the loop seam (50 ms of zeros at the head, a 20 ms tail fade), every 8 s, in what is otherwise a near-continuous rustle. Masked live at the lantern point (no >5 dB periodic dip proven), but audible solo. Same likely cause (a scatter without wrap)."
  },
  {
   "severity": "minor",
   "cue": "amb_fray_lantern",
   "what": "A continuous high-band paper rustle (59 % above 2 kHz, flatness 0.54, a steady floor) that the build gate does not class as a wash, so neither the 25 % HF cap nor the wash swell bar applies to it. By file it peaks 6.9 dB over the FRAY music's quietest frames at 8 kHz, at full on its 8 points. Live it is 19.3-23.9 LU under the music. It reads as hiss, not wind, but it is the one ambience cue with an ungated noise floor. Fix: thin the grain density (220/s -> ~60/s) or class it as a wash."
  },
  {
   "severity": "note",
   "what": "RIFT lane bottom: bed 11.3 LU under the music (bar 11), whole bus 9.7 (bar 8). This is the slimmest live margin, because the RIFT music runs about -31 LUFS there."
  },
  {
